commit 0e03fee81e87e6d6a186fb72610589bd92fc87cd
Author: Tolga Unal <115488770+unaltolga@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Nov 9 11:53:32 2026 -0500

    Read the cents of a dollar amount in the IndexTTS normalizer (#389)
    
    The currency pattern took every digit, comma, period and space after
    "$" and joined the digits, so "$2.50" became "two hundred fifty
    dollars", "$1,299.99" became "one hundred twenty nine thousand nine
    hundred ninety nine dollars", a number after the amount was added to
    it, and the comma or period after the amount was dropped. Match the
    dollars, with commas only between digits, and an optional fraction
    after a decimal point, and read the fraction as cents, as the Python
    normalizer does.

