Author: ahuzmeza <32289581+ahuzmeza@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sat Nov 7 21:51:51 2026 +0200

    VoxCPM2: run bfloat16 checkpoints in bfloat16 (#380)
    
    The rotary tables, the masks and audio features, and the DiT's noise and time
    embeddings are float32, so a bfloat16 checkpoint ran in float32 from start to
    end. As the reference does, the rotation is computed in float32 and cast back,
    and the rest uses the model's dtype. The VAE stays float32.
    
    VoxCPM 1 and 1.5 share this code, so their zero-shot runs change too. Their
    voice cloning stays in float32.

