diff --git a/Tests/VoxCPM2DtypeTests.swift b/Tests/VoxCPM2DtypeTests.swift
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a72419f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Tests/VoxCPM2DtypeTests.swift
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+import MLX
+import MLXNN
+import Testing
+
+@testable import MLXAudioTTS
+
+struct VoxCPM2DtypeTests {
+    private static func tinyConfig() -> VoxCPM2LMConfig {
+        VoxCPM2LMConfig(
+            hiddenSize: 32, numHiddenLayers: 1, numAttentionHeads: 4, numKeyValueHeads: 2,
+            intermediateSize: 64, vocabSize: 16,
+            ropeLongFactor: [1, 1, 1, 1], ropeShortFactor: [1, 1, 1, 1]
+        )
+    }
+
+    private static func toBFloat16(_ module: Module) {
+        let params = module.parameters().flattened().map {
+            ($0.0, $0.1.dtype.isFloatingPoint ? $0.1.asType(.bfloat16) : $0.1)
+        }
+        module.update(parameters: ModuleParameters.unflattened(params))
+    }
+
+    @Test func lmKeepsWeightDtypeThroughRotaryEmbedding() {
+        let lm = VoxMiniCPMModel(Self.tinyConfig())
+        Self.toBFloat16(lm)
+
+        let (hidden, cache) = lm(inputsEmbeds: MLXRandom.normal([1, 5, 32]).asType(.bfloat16))
+        #expect(hidden.dtype == .bfloat16)
+        #expect(cache[0].0.dtype == .bfloat16)
+    }
+
+    @Test func ditSamplesInConditioningDtype() {
+        let config = Self.tinyConfig()
+        let cfm = VoxUnifiedCFM(
+            inChannels: 4, cfmParams: VoxCPM2CFMConfig(),
+            estimator: VoxCPMLocDiT(config, inChannels: 4)
+        )
+        Self.toBFloat16(cfm)
+
+        let mu = MLXRandom.normal([1, 64]).asType(.bfloat16)
+        let cond = MLXRandom.normal([1, 4, 2])
+        #expect(cond.dtype == .float32)
+        let feat = cfm.sample(mu: mu, nTimesteps: 4, patchSize: 2, cond: cond, cfgValue: 2.0)
+        #expect(feat.dtype == .bfloat16)
+    }
+}

commit 373644559fe15f3e8a4d3f68d36b94a111e66dbb
Author: Tom Vaucourt <34662901+T0mSIlver@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sat Nov 7 11:48:06 2026 -0800

    NemotronASR: add Nemotron Unified (#374)
    
    * Nemotron ASR: support Nemotron Unified with buffered streaming
    
    nvidia/nemotron-labs-unified-asr-0.6b has the same NeMo class as Nemotron 3.5
    but a non-causal encoder (BatchNorm conv, input scaling, biased projections)
    and the chunked_limited_with_rc attention mask. It streams buffered: each step
    re-encodes left context + chunk + right context, as NeMo's
    speech_to_text_streaming_infer_rnnt.py does.
    
    - Conformer: non-causal subsampling and padding masks as in NeMo, BatchNorm
      conv, rc mask
    - Audio: per_feature normalization over NeMo's samples / hop valid frames
    - NemotronASRBufferedEncoder: NeMo's buffer bookkeeping for files and live
      sessions
    - generate: full context up to 60 s, then 10/10/5 s buffered; generateStream
      and makeStreamSession stream buffered; chunkMs is the latency (160-2080 ms)
    
    * mlx-audio-swift-stt: stream Unified checkpoints through the session
    
    * Nemotron ASR README: Nemotron Unified
    
    * Nemotron Unified: encode chunks that become ready together as one batch
    
    A step that follows a slow one, or a whole file, completes several chunks at
    once. Their windows share length, left context and mask, so they encode as
    one batch of up to 16 instead of one pass each.
    
    * Nemotron Unified: drop the startup ramp's buffers once the window is full
    
    Until the left context fills, each step's window is a new size and MLX's
    buffer cache keeps every size's buffers: on a MacBook the cache reached the
    helper's 2 GB limit within the first 5.6 s. From then on every window has
    one size, so clear the cache once there.
    
    * Nemotron Unified: compile the encoder for full-size windows
    
    Every window after the left context fills has one shape, so the encoder is
    compiled per batch size for those; ramp and last windows run uncompiled.
    
    * Nemotron Unified: build the mel window and filterbank once per session
    
    * Nemotron Unified: no zero-frame chunks; latency and language rules as NeMo
    
    - A stop with under one hop of new audio left a zero-frame last chunk.
    - Any latency rounds to 80 ms frames within 160-2080 ms; the chunk comes from
      NVIDIA's table row at or below it, the rest is right context (was: snap to
      the nearest row).
    - Language prompts resolve as NeMo's: exact key, else a bare code with exactly
      one locale key. NeMo raises otherwise; this non-throwing API warns once and
      uses the default language.
    
    * Nemotron ASR README: Unified latency and language rules
    
    * Nemotron Unified: trace the compiled encoder once per model and shape
    
    It was cached per session, so every dictation traced again at its first full
    window.
    
    * Nemotron Unified: integer divisions in the rc mask and subsampling lengths
    
    MLX's `/` on integer arrays is true division in float32. The rc mask's chunk
    start was therefore the frame itself, so every chunk over one frame (560 ms
    and up, offline long-form) saw a sliding window instead of NeMo's chunk-aligned
    one; and the non-causal subsampling kept one padded frame at each stride for
    even lengths. Both now use floorDivide.
    
    * Nemotron Unified: clear the cache after each ramp step, not once
    
    Clearing once at the first full window left the ramp's peak: the cache still
    reached 1.98 GB in the first 5.6 s on a MacBook, though it held 146 MB at
    60 s. Clearing after each growing window bounds it by one step's buffers.
    
    * NemotronASR: makeStreamSession(language:bufferedContext:) for Unified
    
    An app can pick the buffer layout (left, chunk, right) instead of NVIDIA's
    latency table, e.g. a 160 ms chunk or a 2.8 s left context, which cut a
    MacBook step from 68.6 ms to 26.1 ms at the same 320 ms latency.
    
    * NemotronASR Unified: token parity with NeMo on media/false-turn.wav
    
    NeMo fp32 token ids at five latencies; fp32 compute must match exactly,
    bfloat16 within a 3 % edit rate. Runs only with a converted checkpoint
    (NEMOTRON_UNIFIED_MLX_PATH) and the MLX runtime tests enabled.
    
    * NemotronASR Unified tests: text only grows at every chunk size; interleaved encoders share no state
    
    Covers chunks of 2 and 7 frames and full compiled windows, which the session
    tests did not reach, and two encoders with different layouts and languages
    using the model's shape-keyed compiled encoders in turn.
    
    * NemotronASR Unified: NeMo's -1e4 mask value, finite in float16
    
    With -1e9 the mask is -inf in float16, so a query row with every key masked
    (a padded chunk under a left-0 layout) turned NaN, and later layers spread it
    to valid frames. Unreachable at speechd's layouts; reachable through an
    explicit bufferedContext.
    
    * README: Nemotron Unified 8-bit in the model table and the NemotronASR example
    
    * NemotronASR Unified: tests run in CI; caller errors throw, not trap
    
    The 12 Unified tests move to NemotronUnifiedTests on tiny models with no
    runtime-test opt-in, so CI runs them. makeStreamSession(language:bufferedContext:)
    and NemotronASRBufferedContext(left:chunk:right:) throw
    NemotronASRStreamingError for a cache-aware checkpoint or an invalid layout,
    where they trapped. The two lock-guarded statics say so. The module README
    documents the explicit layout and how to rerun the NeMo parity test.
    
    * NemotronASR Unified: the long-form layout uses the unchecked initializer
    
    * NemotronASR Unified: prompt-language table against NeMo for every key
    
    NeMo's resolve_prompt_index on the Unified checkpoint's 118 prompt keys, bare
    codes and case variants; where NeMo raises, the port uses the default language.
    
    * Nemotron Unified: drop guards that cannot fire, keep buffered audio in MLX
    
    - resolvePromptIndex: no warn-once state; an unmatched language uses the default prompt
    - defaultBufferedContext builds the layout directly from the config
    - forLatency: no force-unwraps
    - attention visibility: only the offline [-1, -1, -1] context skips the chunk mask
    - per-feature normalization: drop the clamp and condition that never apply
    - the buffered encoder holds its audio as an MLXArray; offline and generateStream no longer round-trip through [Float]
    - comments: say the behaviour, not where it was ported from
    
    * Nemotron Unified: point the docs at the mlx-community checkpoints
    
    * Nemotron Unified README: the bf16 repo is named -bf16
    
    * NemotronASR Unified: default to the 320 ms layout when the config has none
    
    A Unified config without default_att_context_size fell back to the
    encoder's training context, [-1, -1, -1], whose zero-size chunk made a
    stream session loop forever. Default to the converter's [70, 1, 3].
    
    * NemotronASR Unified: drop the compiled-encoder cache
    
    On a Mac mini M2, compiling the encoder for full windows saved 1-3.5 % per
    step with bf16 weights and under 1.5 % with 8-bit (median of 4 interleaved
    rounds, 40 s, 320 and 1120 ms). Not worth a lock-guarded per-shape cache.
    
    * NemotronASR Unified: drop the full-weight NeMo parity test
    
    CI runners can't load the real checkpoint. Parity was verified offline during
    the port; the remaining tests use tiny random models.
    
    * NemotronASR: stop buffered streaming on cancellation
    
    * CI: serialize MLX tests to avoid runner memory exhaustion
    
    ---------
    
    Co-authored-by: Lucas Newman <lucasnewman@me.com>

