commit 6a898d6063a04cc429d1ff3344219918becf9e70
Author: ahuzmeza <32289581+ahuzmeza@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 3 21:19:51 2026 +0200

    VoxtralTTS: keep 25 codec context frames when streaming (#370)
    
    decodeChunk kept 16 frames of left context, but the codec decoder reaches 21 frames back, so the first frames after every chunk boundary were decoded from truncated history and differed from the offline decode. The reference (vllm-omni codec_left_context_frames) uses 25.
    
    Real Voxtral-4B-TTS-2603 4-bit, streamed vs offline decode of the same codes: max abs diff 1.8e-4 to 1.1e-3 (0.7 to 4.6 % of rms) at 16, at most 1.2e-6 (float noise) at 25. Streams that fit in one chunk are bit-identical in both. No measurable change in time to first audio or total time.
    
    Adds streamedChunksMatchOfflineDecode (fails at 16, passes at 25).

