commit 0dda61b29c308175e302dceef77c3bd84551e92b
Author: ahuzmeza <32289581+ahuzmeza@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sun Nov 1 00:54:59 2026 +0200

    Canary: decode long audio in chunks (#364)
    
    Canary encoded and decoded a whole recording in one pass. On longer clips the decoder drifts and stops early: on a 72 s clip it rewrote a sentence and dropped the last ~50 words. `chunkDuration` was in the default parameters (1200) but unused.
    
    A waveform longer than `chunkDuration` is now split at low-energy points with the shared `splitAudioIntoChunks` (as Qwen3-ASR, Cohere Transcribe, FunASR and Mega-ASR do), each chunk decoded on its own with `maxTokens` per chunk, and the texts joined with per-chunk segments. The default `chunkDuration` is 30 s, the STT CLI's default. Shorter audio and precomputed features keep the single pass.
    
    Mediform/canary-1b-v2-mlx-q8, `--language en`, Release CLI on a Mac mini M2 Pro, word error rate:
    - 72 s, 242 words, 16 distinct sentences (macOS `say`): one pass 0.273 -> 30 s chunks 0.029.
    - 88 s, 225 words (TTS clips joined): 0.369 -> 0.053.
    A 25 s clip and five single-sentence clips: identical output.
    
    Test: 40 s of audio in 10 s chunks is decoded in at least three passes (fails before the change).

