commit abd013560ded3b79a2062873225999fd6a4f0b78
Author: ahuzmeza <32289581+ahuzmeza@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 31 21:31:47 2026 +0200

    FireRedASR2: decode long audio in chunks (#362)
    
    FireRedASR2 ran one beam search over the whole recording. On longer recordings it drops sentences and loops: on a 72 s clip it skipped a sentence and ended repeating fragments ("to put out to put out ..."); on an 88 s clip it returned 164 of 225 words.
    
    A waveform longer than `chunkDuration` is now split at low-energy points with the shared `splitAudioIntoChunks` (as Qwen3-ASR, Cohere Transcribe, FunASR and Mega-ASR do), each chunk decoded with the same beam search, and the texts joined with per-chunk segments. The default `chunkDuration` is 30 s, the STT CLI's default. Shorter audio, multi-channel input and the explicit `generate(audio:beamSize:...)` keep the single pass.
    
    mlx-community/FireRedASR2-AED-mlx, `--language en`, Release CLI on a Mac mini M2 Pro, word error rate:
    - 72 s, 242 words, 16 distinct sentences (macOS `say`): 0.421 -> 0.008.
    - 88 s, 225 words (TTS clips joined): 0.364 -> 0.089.
    Five single-sentence clips: identical output.
    
    Test: 40 s of audio in 10 s chunks is decoded in at least three passes (fails before the change).

