Author: Tom Vaucourt <34662901+T0mSIlver@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 31 12:11:34 2026 -0700

    Mel spectrogram: drop the last centred frame, as WhisperFeatureExtractor does (#363)
    
    computeMelSpectrogram kept every frame of the reflect-padded STFT, so it
    returned one frame more than WhisperFeatureExtractor and Python mlx-audio,
    and took the -8 clamp's max over that extra frame. Qwen3-ASR, the Qwen3
    forced aligner and GLM-ASR all use it. On a 565 s chunk, that one frame is
    what makes Qwen3-ASR-1.7B-4bit repeat its last sentence instead of stopping.

