commit fb829f59fcfbe16e35a77a2a62ff46c0a53b3460
Author: ahuzmeza <32289581+ahuzmeza@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 31 21:06:49 2026 +0200

    Canary: accept language names as well as codes (#361)
    
    The STT CLI turns "en" into "English" (`normalizeLanguage`), and Canary looked up `<|English|>` as a prompt token. No such token exists, so both language tokens were dropped without a warning, and the model chose the language itself: an English clip came back mixing about nine European languages (Croatian, Polish, Russian, Greek, Czech, Finnish and others), sometimes ending in a repetition loop. Any caller passing a name ("German") had the same result.
    
    `CanaryConfig.languageCode(for:)` maps a name to one of the model's supported language codes by its English name (Foundation `Locale`) and a region-qualified code ("en-US") to its language; codes and unknown values pass through unchanged.
    
    Mediform/canary-1b-v2-mlx-q8, Release CLI on a Mac mini M2 Pro, a 25 s English clip and five single-sentence clips (166 words), word error rate:
    - `--language en`: 12.3 (2040 errors, mostly the loop) -> 0.072, the same as without the flag.
    - `--language German`: same failure before; now resolves to `de` and returns German, as Canary does when source and target are German.
    
    Test: names, codes, region-qualified codes and an unsupported name resolve as expected.

