commit e1b473e3c69d54fd1bd5eed5e3b670a9299ed657
Author: ahuzmeza <32289581+ahuzmeza@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 31 19:52:36 2026 +0200

    English G2P: read numbers as misaki does (#353)
    
    - EnglishNum2Word had no tens word for 20, so 21-29 lost it: 25 read as "five", 221 as "two hundred one", 21st as "first", 2023 as "twenty three".
    - It tried thousands before millions, so 1000000 read as "one thousand thousand".
    - extend_num split num2words output on spaces only, so "twenty-one" stayed one word; misaki splits on any non-letter.
    - Decimals such as 2.5 went to the acronym speller and came out empty; misaki only spells words whose letters are all alphabetic. They are converted through Decimal(string:), since Decimal(Double) turns 19.99 into 19.98999999999999488.
    - % & @ are tagged as punctuation by NLTagger and were dropped; they are now read as in misaki's symbol table.
    - A currency sign before a decimal ($3.50) was forgotten because NLTagger does not tag 3.50 as a number.

