commit ff1427a1eefb652767a7bd4431825d0c62e99990
Author: ahuzmeza <32289581+ahuzmeza@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 31 19:51:42 2026 +0200

    Qwen3-TTS: fix reference audio ignored when no transcript is given (#352)
    
    * Qwen3-TTS: compute the speaker-encoder mel like the reference
    
    extractSpeakerEmbedding fed the ECAPA speaker encoder the shared
    Whisper-style mel (power, HTK scale, log10 normalization, centered STFT).
    The reference mel_spectrogram uses magnitude, Slaney scale up to 12 kHz,
    natural log and a (n_fft - hop) / 2 reflect pad. Add a matching
    speakerEncoderMelSpectrogram, tested against values computed in Python.
    
    * Qwen3-TTS: use the reference-audio x-vector when no transcript is given
    
    With refAudio and no refText, generation fell through to
    prepareGenerationInputs, which dropped the audio, so the voice was
    generic. Match Python _prepare_generation_inputs: inject the speaker
    embedding of refAudio into the codec prefix (Base models; CustomVoice
    speaker ids unchanged). The embedding is cast to the prefix dtype, as in
    Blaizzy/mlx-audio#879, so the float32 speaker encoder output does not
    promote the decode to float32.

