commit 200ced1bdcefbe1b84f33e79e9df9f2501ebb1dc
Author: ahuzmeza <32289581+ahuzmeza@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 31 01:17:03 2026 +0200

    Mimi: fix attention seeing past its context window (PocketTTS cloning drops the first word) (#357)
    
    * Mimi transformer: limit attention to the context window within a chunk
    
    Attention trimmed old keys after the cache update but masked only causally,
    so in a call with more frames than `context` the later queries could see
    further back than the window. Python masks 0 <= delta < context. Single-step
    calls also kept context + 1 keys; they now keep `context`, as in Python, and
    multi-frame decode steps (PocketTTS, Mimi streaming) go through the same mask.
    
    The Mimi transformer is shared by several models. PocketTTS encodes a
    reference clip in one call, with SEANet at 200 Hz, so the 250-frame window is
    1.25 s and any longer clip was encoded wrongly:
    
    - PocketTTS voice embedding vs Python (5 s / 10 s / 12 s / 13 s clips):
      relative error 31% / 45% / 49% / 52% before, 1.4e-6 to 2.8e-6 after
    - PocketTTS --ref_audio, 13 s reference: "The" was missing in 10 of 10 runs
      before and said in 10 of 10 after (Python: 5 of 5)
    - Qwen3-TTS Base cloning (ICL and x-vector), 13 s reference: complete
      sentence before and after (its encoder window of 250 frames is 10 s)
    
    Adds a test checking that each position's output equals a fresh run over its
    window, and that 1/3/5-frame chunked streaming equals the one-shot call.
    
    * Allow Metal precision differences in Mimi attention tests
    
    ---------
    
    Co-authored-by: Lucas Newman <lucasnewman@me.com>

