commit 1edbcc108ce131475d25125ac4bdcc998fc5d520
Author: ahuzmeza <32289581+ahuzmeza@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 31 00:54:43 2026 +0200

    Soprano: read ordinals as ordinals (#358)
    
    The K/M/B/T suffix rule matched any digit followed by one of those letters, ignoring case, so the t of 4th, 20th or 111th was read as trillion ("july four trillionh"). It now matches a whole number with the suffix as a word, as in Soprano's own text normalizer. Ordinals above 100 appended th to the cardinal (101st "one hundred oneth"); the last two digits now go through the under-100 ordinal path. Same change as Python mlx-audio's text.py port.

